# 11. Candidate Resilience Metrics

The following metrics are proposed for investigation.

## Recovery Time

Time from disruption to restoration of normal operation.

## Recovery Success

Whether the node successfully returns to its expected operational state.

## Synchronisation Recovery

Time required for the node to return to the expected chain state.

## Availability

Percentage of time the node is operational during the experiment.

## Data Integrity

Whether blockchain data remains valid and consistent following disruption.

## Resource Consumption

CPU, memory, storage and bandwidth utilisation.

## Human Intervention

The degree of manual intervention required.

## Recovery Complexity

The number and complexity of steps required to restore operation.

These metrics are preliminary.

The research must determine whether they are meaningful, measurable and comparable.

