# 15. Preliminary Findings

The initial review leads to five preliminary findings.

## Finding 1

Bitcoin resilience is not an unexplored research field.

Network-level and physical infrastructure resilience are already being investigated.

## Finding 2

Bitcoin node resource behaviour is also an active research area.

Therefore, BNSAT-R must avoid simply reproducing existing performance benchmarks.

## Finding 3

Multiple mature projects already address node deployment, management and monitoring.

Therefore, building another general-purpose node management platform would likely be poorly differentiated.

## Finding 4

There may be a narrower opportunity around the systematic measurement of individual node recovery behaviour under controlled disruptions.

This requires significantly more research before being considered a validated gap.

## Finding 5

The strongest potential contribution may be methodological rather than purely software-based.

UBRO may be able to contribute:

* Experimental methodology;
* Benchmarking;
* Reproducible test protocols;
* Open-source measurement tools;
* Research datasets;
* Technical documentation.

